resource_plural() is a derived/declared read-only identity accessor with the same swallow-an-argument shape karr #67 fixed for kind()/api_version(). karr #67 scoped itself to the two most-called accessors and deliberately left resource_plural untouched.

Sources, mirroring #67:
- IO::K8s::Role::APIObject::resource_plural -- derived read-only method, no @_ guard.
- IO::K8s::APIObject import: resource_plural import-param installed as sub { $plural } (no guard).
- IO::K8s::AutoGen: resource_plural GVK constant sub { $res_plural } (no guard).

Fix: same one-line "@_ > 1 -> croak" guard in all three spots, message "resource_plural is fixed for this class and cannot be set" (role: "derived from the class name"). Behaviour change -> Changes entry. Low priority: resource_plural is called far less than kind/api_version.

Found while implementing karr #67 (fail-closed on kind/api_version).
Lane: io-k8s-worker.
